0	99	Jessika Roswall (born Vilhelmsson, 18 December 1972) is a Swedish politician of the Moderate Party.
100	262	She serves as European Commissioner for Environment, Water Resilience and a Competitive Circular Economy and Swedish European Commissioner since 1 December 2024.

262	400	She served as Minister for European Union Affairs and Minister for Nordic Cooperation in the cabinet of Ulf Kristersson from 2022 to 2024.
401	508	She was also a member of parliament from the 2010 general election to 2024, representing Uppsala County.



508	607	Early life and education
Roswall is the daughter of lawyer Anders Roswall; her mother is a teacher.
608	704	She graduated from high school in 1991 and studied history at Stockholm University in 1995–1997.
705	799	She moved to Uppsala to study law at Uppsala University and graduated in law (LLM) in 2002.



799	895	Career
After graduation, Roswall started working as a paralegal at the law firm Wigert & Placht.
896	963	She then became a lawyer, specializing in criminal and family law.

963	1040	At the same time, Roswall was a deputy in the municipal council of Enköping.

1040	1140	In the 2010 parliamentary election, Roswall was elected member of parliament for the Moderate Party.
1141	1225	As a newly appointed member of parliament, she became a member of the tax committee.
1226	1356	Since 2011, she has been a member of the Civil Affairs Committee, where she works with consumer policy issues, among other things.
1357	1450	Since 2015, she has also been a member of the Swedish Consumer Agency's transparency council.
1451	1512	She became her party's spokesperson on EU relations in 2019.

1512	1631	From 18 October 2022, Roswall served as Minister for EU Affairs and for Nordic Cooperation in the Kristersson Cabinet.

1631	1817	Following the 2024 European elections, the Swedish government nominated Roswall as the country's European Commissioner, on 8 August 2024, serving under President Ursula von der Leyen.



